{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>You shall not profane.</b> To transgress My words deliberately. Since it is said ״וְלֹא תְחַלְּלוּ״ — what is taught by ״וְנִקְדַּשְׁתִּי״? Surrender yourself and sanctify My name. One might say this applies to an individual — therefore it says <b>in the midst of the children of Israel.</b> And when one surrenders himself, he must surrender himself on condition to die, for whoever surrenders himself on condition of a miracle — they do not perform a miracle for him. For so we find with Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah, that they did not surrender themselves on condition of a miracle, as it says (Daniel 3): ״וְהֵן לָא יְדִיעַ לֶהֱוֵא לָךְ מַלְכָּא״ and so forth — whether He rescues or does not rescue — ״יְדִיעַ לֶהֱוֵא לָךְ״ and so forth (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:51.876998147Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}